# ============================================================================
# DriveAI — Colección de pruebas de API (REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
#
# Uso en VS Code:  instala la extensión "REST Client" (humanitec).
# Uso en IntelliJ: abre el archivo con "HTTP Request".
#   - Backend en http://localhost:8080.
#   - Ejecuta las requests en orden: el login guarda el token en @customerToken.
#   - El carrito y las órdenes se resuelven desde el JWT: NO se envía sessionId.
# ============================================================================

@host = http://localhost:8080
@email = api-demo-{{$timestamp}}@driveai.test
@password = ApiDemoPassw0rd!
@customerToken = REEMPLAZAR_CON_TOKEN
@adminToken = REEMPLAZAR_CON_TOKEN_ADMIN
@carId = 1
@cartItemId = 1
@orderId = 1

### 1. Healthcheck del backend
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### 2. Catálogo paginado (público)
GET {{host}}/api/cars?page=0&size=12

### 3. Filtros combinados (rango de precio + híbrido + SUV)
GET {{host}}/api/cars?minPrice=20000&maxPrice=40000&fuelType=HIBRIDO&bodyType=SUV&sort=price,asc

### 4. Detalle de vehículo (público) — 200 + ETag
GET {{host}}/api/cars/{{carId}}

### 5. Detalle inexistente — 404 Problem Details
GET {{host}}/api/cars/99999999

### 6. Registro de cliente — 201
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "fullName": "Cliente API"
}

### 7. Login de cliente — 200 (copiar token a @customerToken)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 8. Login con contraseña incorrecta — 401
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "PasswordIncorrecta!"
}

### 9. Carrito sin token — 401
GET {{host}}/api/cart

### 10. Agregar al carrito (dueño = JWT)
POST {{host}}/api/cart/add
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carId": {{carId}},
  "quantity": 1
}

### 11. Ver mi carrito
GET {{host}}/api/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 12. Actualizar cantidad de un ítem propio
PUT {{host}}/api/cart/update/{{cartItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 2
}

### 13. Checkout idempotente (Idempotency-Key)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-idempotency-key-001

{
  "items": [
    { "carId": {{carId}}, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 14. Repetir el mismo checkout con la misma Idempotency-Key — misma orden
POST {{host}}/api/orders/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-idempotency-key-001

{
  "items": [
    { "carId": {{carId}}, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 15. Historial propio de órdenes
GET {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 16. Detalle de una orden propia
GET {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 17. Cancelar una orden propia — 200
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 18. Cancelar de nuevo — 409 transición inválida
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 19. Cliente intenta crear un auto — 403 (BFLA)
POST {{host}}/api/cars
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "Hack",
  "model": "Forbidden",
  "year": 2024,
  "price": 1,
  "mileage": 0,
  "fuelType": "GASOLINA",
  "fuelConsumption": 1,
  "transmission": "MANUAL",
  "bodyType": "SEDAN",
  "imageUrl": "https://img.test/x.jpg",
  "description": "No permitido",
  "stock": 1
}

### 20. Cotización SOAP (fallback controlado si el proveedor falla)
GET {{host}}/api/soap/quote/{{carId}}

### 21. Asesor IA (requiere GROQ_API_KEY; sin clave devuelve 503 controlado)
POST {{host}}/api/ai/recommend
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "Busco una SUV híbrida familiar por menos de 30000 dólares",
  "sessionId": "api-demo-session"
}

### 22. Documento OpenAPI
GET {{host}}/v3/api-docs
